Z||000000||geyser||09-04-2001||01:13 AM||||Could someone provide the GM part numbers for the clutch slave and master cylinders? I'm about to rework the entire system as my clutch gave out on the way to work the other day. Thanks in advance. PS I'm going for the centerforce dual friction and TO bearing after reading all the past threads.||||reg||5
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||09-04-2001||08:28 AM||||Slave cylinder depends on what kind of tranny you are using.  I'm not sure about the Master, that's probably all the same.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wade87GT||09-04-2001||12:52 PM||||Try the search here, I went through the same thing several months ago and got the PNs from someone. I ordered my stuff through <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A>  and got them a lot cheaper than anyplace else.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||09-04-2001||01:26 PM||||From memory the 4-speed and Isuzu share the same slave cylinder.  The slave for the Getrag is different and it's a lot more expensive.<P>There are 2 different master cylinders, the difference is whether the hose attaches in front of or behind the resevoir.  <P>If you've got an '84-'85 you should have a 1st gen master cylinder, if you've got an '87-'88 you should have a 2nd gen unit.  If you have an '86 you have to physically inspect the existing master to see where the hose fits.<P>Some literature refers to a 3rd gen unit, but from memory it's the same part # as the 2nd gen unit, they just attach a bit differently in the back.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||09-04-2001||08:57 PM||||This is the only master cylinder pn I can find in stock :10142033 <BR> <P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
